  "worked_solution": "First, we calculate the velocity vector $v.$ Differentiating the position vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\u27e8\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e8\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(2t)),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(4t))\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e8-4\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(2t),4\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(4t)\u27e9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the velocity when $t=\\frac{\\pi }{2},$ we substitute in the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & =\u27e8-4\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(\\pi ),4\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(2\\pi )\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e8-4(0),4(1)\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e80,4\u27e9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the speed at $t=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ we calculate the magnitude of $v(\\frac{\\pi }{2}),$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|v(\\frac{\\pi }{2})| & =\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16} \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
